LocalRouter's change to plotarmordev/drama-tensorfold's recipe/pilot_macos.py (Apache License 2.0, Copyright 2026
plotarmordev), at db6ba7da314b24b42b02978ba4401f54f6738311. It adds --external-admission: when an outer scheduler
(LocalRouter) admits the load from its own memory budget, the launcher skips its free+inactive admission
(max(weights + 30 GiB, 34 GiB)) and its 34 GiB abort; the lock and the process-group cleanup are unchanged. It adds
--parent-pid PID: macOS has no parent-death signal, so the launcher stops the server, as for SIGTERM, once PID is no
longer its parent (the worker was killed). And it imports weight_selection from its own directory, so it runs under
python3 -I (which leaves the script's directory off sys.path). TENSORFOLD_MEMORY_RESERVE_GIB is left alone: only the
CUDA build reads it. This patch is licensed under the Apache License 2.0. setup-macos.sh applies it with `git apply`
to a copy at ROOT/launcher/pilot_macos.py.

